# Cache files written by the GitHub Actions polling workflow every 15 minutes
# and by `yarn poll:*` locally, so two sides diverge constantly.
#
# The default text merge writes conflict markers into the JSON, which corrupts a
# venue cache outright. `merge=ours` (the previous rule) avoids that but keeps
# the local copy and discards the other side's history, and several of these
# platforms cannot re-fetch the past.
#
# This driver unions both sides by session id, so a session that has already run
# can never be lost. See scripts/merge-venue-cache.mjs.
#
# Requires one-time setup per clone: yarn cache:setup
src/data/venues/*.json merge=venuecache
